  "description": "VOJNAN crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P n -3 n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H154 O42 Yb9 1+,Cl1 1-,21(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2A (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2B (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2C (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2E (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2H (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2R (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2S (Yb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.545-5.013 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.34-167.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C160H154ClO42Yb9. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
